status: active
goal: Audit and fix backtest realism issues — cap_multiplier allowing unbounded position sizes vs ADV, and parameter overfitting quantification. Ensure backtested Calmar/returns are closer to what live trading would produce.
started: 2026-03-15
type: research+implementation
trigger: |
  Quant review (2026-03-15) found 6 red flags inflating backtested Calmar by ~100-1000x.
  User confirmed compounding (#1) and DD measurement (#2) are acceptable.
  Survivorship bias (#5) is accepted.
  Remaining issues to address:
    - cap_multiplier=15 on some strategies effectively disables ADV caps
    - 5% ADV cap may still be insufficient at scale (need to verify)
    - Parameter overfitting not quantified across strategy suite

phases:
  phase1_cap_audit:
    name: "ADV cap effectiveness audit"
    status: pending
    tasks:
      - Survey all strategies for cap_multiplier values
      - For each strategy, compute max position size vs token ADV at various equity levels ($200K, $1M, $10M, $50M)
      - Verify the 5% ADV cap actually binds (cap = strategy_equity * cap_pct * cap_multiplier — if cap_multiplier is high, does ADV cap still dominate?)
      - Identify strategies where positions would exceed 5% of daily volume
      - Recommend cap_multiplier adjustments per strategy

  phase2_capacity_analysis:
    name: "Strategy capacity limits"
    status: pending
    tasks:
      - For top portfolios (4-edge, s60, s58+s65), compute equity level where ADV constraints start binding
      - Model expected slippage at various equity levels using simple market impact (sqrt model)
      - Estimate realistic capacity ceiling per portfolio
      - Document per-token concentration at current paper equity levels

  phase3_overfitting_quantification:
    name: "Parameter sensitivity & overfitting"
    status: pending
    tasks:
      - For each Tier A/B strategy, run +/-20% parameter perturbation on key params
      - Measure Calmar degradation under perturbation (>30% = fragile)
      - Compare in-sample vs out-of-sample performance windows
      - Compute walk-forward efficiency (WFE) for strategies not yet measured
      - Flag strategies with WFE < 50% or high parameter sensitivity

done_when:
  - All strategies have appropriate cap_multiplier values
  - ADV cap effectiveness verified at realistic equity levels
  - Capacity ceiling documented per portfolio
  - Parameter sensitivity results for all active strategies
  - Findings recorded in strategy-findings.jsonl
